        {
          "name": "Google Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"logs in with Google\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "if (res && res.data && res.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", res.data.refreshToken || \"\");",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"idToken\": \"{{supabase_service_role_api_key_18pn}}sudR1FAO5GgNcF9dp24J49VkMfkWtkpxRau_srZA6jCEVj896Vhe5PVaHw8oeHh5oWg8Rets9lhvkBuxxa8Zq-LODS0I9mLgbpyYKKthvOa3sl9mGTvquvbfGWYmwMxF3DHDxxzjxGkVFMZxF3-Yi585XE38cMy1kMHn8JQTF7NhFQ67EJAp78q27JFgZjiQ_ybbG4X9k31lG6zb9pZL2KNLLBlGgg\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/google",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "5000",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "google"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: 200, returning the application's own `accessToken` / `refreshToken` (both in the body and as cookies).\n\nThree resolution paths, in order:\n1. **Known `googleId`** — resolved by the stable `sub` claim, never by email, because a Google email can change and `sub` cannot.\n2. **Matching email on an existing account** — links it: sets `googleId`, forces `emailVerified: true`, and flips `authProvider` to `GOOGLE` *only* if the account had no password. An existing password is preserved. Role and status always come from the database, never from Google.\n3. **New email** — provisions `User` (`role: PATIENT`, `password: null`, `authProvider: GOOGLE`, `emailVerified: true`, `image` from the `picture` claim) plus its `Patient` row in one transaction.\n\nAccount standing is checked on every path, including before the link-write, so a blocked or deleted account is refused without being mutated."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "refresh-token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/refresh-token",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "5000",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "refresh-token"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "All seven endpoints under `/api/v1/auth`. Protected routes (`/me`, `/change-password`, `/logout`) are gated by `checkAuth(ADMIN, DOCTOR, PATIENT, SUPER_ADMIN)` — every role passes, so the gate is really just \"authenticated\"."
    },
